///| SFTP protocol version 3 (draft-ietf-secsh-filexfer-01.txt)
///
/// A separate package for the same reason `src/channel` is one: this is pure
/// byte assembly with no socket and no transport, so `cmd/sftp_test` can drive
/// whole request/response exchanges against vectors on all four backends
/// instead of only the one that has a TCP stack.
///
/// The framing is *not* SSH packet framing. There is no padding, no
/// padding-length byte and no message-type byte in the outer header:
///
///     uint32   length      -- of everything after this field
///     byte     type
///     ...      type-specific fields
///
/// transcribed from `send_msg` / `get_msg_extended` (sftp-client.c:151-210).
/// Two details there are load-bearing and easy to get wrong:
///
///   * `put_u32(mlen, sshbuf_len(m))` -- the length does **not** count itself.
///   * both sides use `atomicio6`, which loops until it has read exactly the
///     requested count. A packet is therefore *not* required to fit inside one
///     CHANNEL_DATA, and one CHANNEL_DATA may carry several packets. The
///     framing is a byte stream layered on a byte stream, and `SftpInbuf` in
///     stream.mbt is where that gets reassembled.
import {
  "openssh/openssh_moonbit/src/sshwire",
}

pkgtype(kind: "library")
